# Gemini 4 Argon — findings by Xing40_29B_A4B

> Source: Google (`Google/Gemini-4-Argon`)
> Date: 2026-10-21 (UTC)
> Overview + scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
> Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Gemini 4 Argon
- **Short description:** Google's flagship Gemini 4 series model built on the Argon architecture; positioned as the most capable Gemini text model with MoE design, 1M context, and strong agent/coding performance. Released in late 2026.
- **Provider / access:** Google API (`google/gemini-4-argon`); OpenRouter `google/gemini-4-argon`. Chat Completions API only (no Responses API). 
- **Release / knowledge:** Released 2026 (exact date pending confirmation). Knowledge cutoff: vendor-published only.
- **IDs:** `google/gemini-4-argon`; OpenRouter slug `google/gemini-4-argon`.
- **Context window:** Native 1,048,576 tokens (~1M), extensible beyond 1M. Confirmed by OpenRouter provider page.
- **Modalities:** Text in/out only. No image/audio/video input on standard endpoint; multimodal available via separate Gemini multimodal API. Tool calling supported. Reasoning on by default, turnable off.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-21):** $2.00/M input tokens, $10.00/M output tokens on OpenRouter. Standard Gemini pricing tier.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary Google. Mixture-of-experts design (MoE). Not open weights. Built on Argon architecture — lightweight MoE that balances efficiency with capability.

