### Normalized scores (1–100)

Overall = half-up mean of the five quality dims `(Tool + Reasoning + Context + Multimodal + Coding) / 5`. Never include Cost efficiency.

- **Tool use: 78/100.** MoE architecture with tool calling support confirmed by OpenRouter API schema; but no Terminal-Bench/Tau3 numeric score to qualify it — new model, unverified benchmark numbers. Estimate placed in lower-mid band given no independently verified agent benchmarks. Evidence: OpenRouter provider page.
- **Reasoning: 84/100.** Reasoning on by default per OpenRouter; sufficient to claim strong reasoning support. Estimate placed in upper-mid band — headline is a feature declaration, not a measured score. Evidence: OpenRouter provider page.
- **Context window: 92/100.** Native 1M, one of the largest MoE context windows available. Excellent for long-context tasks; mid-band for context alone but dominant when combined with other capabilities. Evidence: OpenRouter provider page.
- **Multimodal: 50/100.** Multimodal capability exists via separate Gemini multimodal API but not priced on standard endpoint; counted at partial credit for visual understanding capability even though not separately exposed. Evidence: OpenRouter API schema.
- **Coding: 74/100.** New model from Google; no independent coding benchmarks found. Anchored on MoE architecture and general positioning. Estimate placed at moderate band; assume 74 ± 8 until independently confirmed. Evidence: architecture info + lack of published scores.
- **Cost efficiency: 40/100.** $2/$10 is competitive with GPT-class but mid-range among frontier proprietary models. Better than Claude Opus pricing but not cheapest. Evidence: OpenRouter provider page.
- **Overall Score: 74/100.** Mean of [Tool 78 + Reasoning 84 + Context 92 + Multimodal 50 + Coding 74] / 5 = 74.0. Strong context window (1M MoE) + competitive pricing ($2/$10), but no independently verified coding/agent benchmarks to distinguish from peers. Best fit: long-context engineering pipelines, repositoried multi-file coding where 1M context matters, and budget-conscious frontier comparisons — but verify against Claude Opus 5/GPT-6 Astra before trusting for top-tier coding work. Downside: multimodal not separately priced; no published coding benchmarks yet.

